<title>USA: PacifiCorp sees 550 MW Wyo. unit up by Thurs.</title>
<headline>PacifiCorp sees 550 MW Wyo. unit up by Thurs.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unit 3 at the Jim Bridger coal-fired power plant near Rock Springs, Wyo., should be back on line by Thursday, a spokeswoman for the plant's operator, PacifiCorp, said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The 550 megawatt (MW) unit tripped off on Saturday due to problems with a fan, added spokeswoman Leslie Blythe.</p>
<p>The Bridger plant also has three other 550 MW units, which are at normal rates.</p>
<p>--Los Angeles bureau, + 1 213 955 6761</p>
